It does NOT cover:

  * src/, include/, assets/, Makefile, tools/, rsp/, ld/, and the other
    files inherited from the GoldenEye 007 decompilation
    (https://github.com/n64decomp/007). The upstream project is published
    without an explicit license; those files are included here on the same
    basis, unmodified except where a PC-port ABI fix is marked `#ifdef PORT`
    and documented in docs/dev/findings.md. This repository is a downstream
    fork of that decompilation with a PC port added on top.

    As is standard for console decompilation projects, some game data is
    present as re-expressed source (animation tables, display lists, data
    tables) inherited verbatim from the upstream repository. The bulk game
    assets -- textures, audio, models, level geometry, in-game text -- are
    NOT included and are extracted from your own ROM at build time.

THIRD-PARTY CODE: DEAR IMGUI
--------------------------------------------------

port/third_party/imgui/ is Dear ImGui 1.92.9b, Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Omar Cornut,
MIT license (port/third_party/imgui/LICENSE.txt). It also contains stb_truetype,
stb_rect_pack and stb_textedit by Sean Barrett (public domain / MIT).
One local edit to the upstream files: imconfig.h disables the file and shell functions. The rest is
the unmodified 1.92.9b release; the build compiles it without the game's include directories (CMakeLists.txt, ge_imgui).
editor/third_party/imgui_backends/ holds the unmodified 1.92.9b SDL2 and OpenGL3 backends
(imgui_impl_sdl2.*, imgui_impl_opengl3.*, imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h) for the mission editor, same
MIT license (editor/third_party/imgui_backends/LICENSE.txt). tools_pc/menuview/backends/ (Win32 and
OpenGL3, a dev tool) holds the unmodified 1.92.9b files too.

